In general, I prefer tiles for the same reasons that Rob said. But I
also like the graphics to be simple and clear. The default 16x16 tiles
for nethack aren't perfect, but I think they're pretty good - and they
are just the right side for the entire level to fit on my screen!

I feel that nethack has a lot of interface problems, so I think we're
in agreement on that, but I don't think it's because of the tiles. For
example, if I step on a square that has between 2 and 5 items on the
ground, then a side window pops up to list the items and I have to
explicitly close it before I regain control of my character. The
really bugs me. I've glanced at the code to see if I can fix it, but
my conclusion (for the time being) is that I don't know how to fix it
easily without potentially messing up compatibility with other OSs. I
have made a couple of minor changes though =97 for example, if you bring
up the inventory for the "eat" command it will only show edible items
now. Same goes for 'zap', etc. I think it's good to not to have to
scroll through your entire inventory to find your wands every time you
want to zap something (and don't remember the letter for the wand you
want).


